[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/supabase/supabase/pulls/46021","id":3694865462,"node_id":"PR_kwDODMpXOc7cOyw2","html_url":"https://github.com/supabase/supabase/pull/46021","diff_url":"https://github.com/supabase/supabase/pull/46021.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/supabase/supabase/pull/46021.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/supabase/supabase/issues/46021","number":46021,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(docker): move hardcoded Realtime DB_ENC_KEY to .env variable","user":{"login":"mandar1045","id":180984698,"node_id":"U_kgDOCsmbeg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180984698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mandar1045","html_url":"https://github.com/mandar1045","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mandar1045/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mandar1045/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mandar1045/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mandar1045/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mandar1045/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mandar1045/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mandar1045/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mandar1045/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mandar1045/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What does this PR do?\n\nMoves the Realtime service's `DB_ENC_KEY` from a hardcoded value in `docker-compose.yml` to a configurable `.env` variable (`REALTIME_DB_ENC_KEY`), matching how every other secret in the self-hosting stack is managed.\n\n## How I found this\n\nI was doing a systematic security audit of the self-hosting Docker configuration, specifically comparing how each secret flows from `.env` → `docker-compose.yml` → container environment. I went through every service block in `docker-compose.yml` and checked whether each secret or encryption key was sourced from a `${VARIABLE}` reference.\n\nEvery single secret in the stack follows the pattern — `POSTGRES_PASSWORD`, `JWT_SECRET`, `SECRET_KEY_BASE`, `VAULT_ENC_KEY`, `PG_META_CRYPTO_KEY`, `S3_PROTOCOL_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET`, etc. — they are all defined in `.env` and interpolated via `${...}` in `docker-compose.yml`.\n\nBut on **line 314** of `docker-compose.yml`, I found this:\n\n```yaml\nDB_ENC_KEY: supabaserealtime\n```\n\nNo `${...}`. No `.env` variable. Just a raw string. It immediately stood out because it breaks the pattern that the entire rest of the file follows.\n\n## Why this is a real problem\n\n`DB_ENC_KEY` is the encryption key that the Realtime service uses to encrypt sensitive columns in its internal database tables. Because this value is hardcoded:\n\n1. **Every self-hosted Supabase instance in the world shares the same encryption key** — the string `supabaserealtime` is public on GitHub. Anyone who knows this (and now everyone does) can decrypt Realtime's encrypted database columns on any self-hosted instance.\n\n2. **There's no way to rotate it without editing `docker-compose.yml`** — unlike every other secret, users can't change this by editing `.env` and restarting. They have to know to go into `docker-compose.yml` itself, which the documentation tells them not to edit.\n\n3. **The `.env` file's header literally says \"YOU MUST CHANGE ALL THE DEFAULT VALUES BELOW\"** — but since `DB_ENC_KEY` was never in `.env`, users who diligently follow this instruction still end up with the hardcoded default.\n\n## What changed\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `docker/.env.example` | Added `REALTIME_DB_ENC_KEY=your-realtime-encryption-key` with a descriptive comment |\n| `docker/docker-compose.yml` | Changed `DB_ENC_KEY: supabaserealtime` → `DB_ENC_KEY: ${REALTIME_DB_ENC_KEY}` |\n\n## Migration note for existing deployments\n\nExisting self-hosted instances upgrading to this version will need to add `REALTIME_DB_ENC_KEY` to their `.env` file. \n\n- To **maintain backward compatibility** with existing encrypted data, set it to `supabaserealtime` (the previous hardcoded value).\n- To **properly secure** the deployment, set it to a new random value — but note this will invalidate any existing encrypted data in Realtime's internal tables, which will be re-created on restart.\n\nThe `generate-keys.sh` utility script should also be updated in a follow-up to generate this key alongside the others.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Linked to a related issue or discussion\n- [x] Tested locally (docker compose config validates correctly)\n- [x] Backward-compatible with migration path documented\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Realtime now reads a configurable database encryption key from the environment, falling back to the previous default when not set.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added docs explaining REALTIME_DB_ENC_KEY, its 16-byte requirement, and how to generate/set it.\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Tooling updated to generate and populate REALTIME_DB_ENC_KEY into local environment examples.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/supabase/supabase/pull/46021?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-16T15:40:07Z","updated_at":"2026-11-06T11:18:14Z","closed_at":"2026-07-01T12:51:03Z","merged_at":"2026-07-01T12:51:03Z","merge_commit_sha":"02ada3efe354f8e87c9e795473d132f735431f86","assignees":[{"login":"aantti","id":56412611,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NDEyNjEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56412611?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aantti","html_